              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "кольцо (koltsó) — \"a ring\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "кольцо (koltsó) is built on old коло, \"a wheel, a circle\" (Vasmer), the root of колесо, \"wheel\". Vasmer relates it to Greek kýklos, \"circle\", and Old Norse hvel, \"wheel\": English wheel is a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
